77... e4 78. fxe4 Ke1 $6 79. e5 f3 80. Bd5 (80. e6 Bd6 (80... f2 $4 81. Bc4
f1=Q+ 82. Bxf1 Kxf1 83. a5 $1 {wins}) 81. Bc4 Kf2 82. Bd5 Ke3 83. Bxf3) 80...
f2 81. Bc4 Kd2 82. a5 $4 {(sealed move) Sources: BCM, Sept 1949, p307; The
Chess Bulletin, Vol. 1 No. 1, 3 Sept 1949} (82. Bf1 $1 Kc3 (82... Ke1 $11) 83.
a5 bxa5 84. e6 a4 85. b6 a3 86. b7 a2 87. b8=Q a1=Q {is a draw according to
Koenig in BCM. Engines claim White is winning after} 88. Qe5+ Bd4 89. Qb5 (89.
Qxg3+ $1 {Stockfish 10 in 2019}) 89... Bf6 90. e7 {but Black can give up the Q
with} Qxf1+ $1 91. Qxf1 Bxe7 92. Qc1+ Kd3 {and it is not clear how White can
force a win.}) 0-1

