17... Qf6 18. Qe2 Rxh2+ {"Your attack had a little more life than I realised,"
ruefully commented my teen-aged opponent, whose record series of championship
wins had yet to begin." (Sources: 'Chess for the Love of It' by A. R. B.
Thomas, Routledge & Kegan Paul 1973, p62; CHESS, Vol.15, no.169, October 1949,
p22, which pointed out that Oliver Penrose pulled off the same tactical finish
against Walsh nine days later in the London-Sydney radio match.} 0-1

